@namespace LineOps.Desk.Primitives

@*
    A spinner: work under way whose length cannot be known.

    The desk's first answer to "in flight" is the 3px band — the pulse strip on a window, the
    progress bar for a named piece of work — and that stays the answer wherever there is a
    band to draw. The spinner is for the place with no room for one: beside a field that is
    checking what was typed, in a small empty state while its first read arrives. It says only
    "something is happening here"; when the work has a denominator, the progress bar is the
    honest control.

    A ring in the hairline colour with one arc in the accent, turning once every 0.8s, at 16px
    beside body text or 20px on its own. It is a status with a name, so a reader hears what is
    under way; the label defaults to "Loading" only because a spinner is often dropped in before
    its caller knows the work's name — say what it is ("Fetching items") whenever you can.

    Under prefers-reduced-motion the ring stops turning and stays drawn, arc and all: the state
    survives without the travel.
*@

<span class="spinner @SizeClass @DeskLayout.ExtraClass(Extra) @Class"
      style="@DeskLayout.MergeStyle(null, Extra)"
      role="status"
      aria-label="@Label"
      @attributes="DeskLayout.WithoutClassAndStyle(Extra)">
    <span class="spinner__ring" aria-hidden="true"></span>
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>Small is 16px, for a line of text; Medium, the default, is 20px. Large is drawn as Medium.</summary>
    [Parameter] public DeskKeySize Size { get; set; } = DeskKeySize.Medium;

    /// <summary>What is under way, as a reader hears it — the verb and its object where they are known.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = "Loading";

    /// <summary>Extra classes, appended last so a one-off can still win.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? Extra { get; set; }

    private string SizeClass => Size == DeskKeySize.Small ? "spinner--sm" : "spinner--md";
}
